                        "sense_id": "43f1295a-4f13-38c7-ab7d-18920372ae82",
                        "entry_id": "52aea89c-4f42-3cb2-973f-4f3e117a0e5e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Valium."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "informal",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8cdb6e29-effb-4626-a9d1-8d068c12808f",
                                "sense_id": "43f1295a-4f13-38c7-ab7d-18920372ae82",
                                "text": "and i must be on that list of people that need to get knocked over with a hammer 'cause vicodin and val don't knock me out."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "388a3a09-ab99-40b0-a4b2-5a7492983654",
                                "sense_id": "43f1295a-4f13-38c7-ab7d-18920372ae82",
                                "text": "I would think though that whatever the reason for a panic attack valium would be great. I know that if my house was on fire and I was on 15mg of val It^([sic]) would take a lot more energy than I had, to panic. ;^)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5b2e2e7-8aee-4d73-92b9-d23ee973eea3",
                                "sense_id": "43f1295a-4f13-38c7-ab7d-18920372ae82",
                                "text": "I'm a medic and phenobarb is the primary drug for true seizures, but the OP states the cat presents seizure like behavior at the sound of her voice. I don't know where any of you are from, but we don't treat seizures with val."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
